{
 "schemaVersion": 1,
 "note": "Can a closed facility still use outside air, and when should a hybrid house shut its curtain and run lamps instead of sunlight? Seven scenarios at Fairbanks, AK (ZIP 99701), the ideal controller, one weather year. The sealed rows sweep the outside-air path from the shipped opaque 2 ACH shell leakage to a designed economizer; the hybrid rows compare running open against closing up, with and without a guard that keeps the shade open while the crop is behind on light. Capacities are declared assumptions held constant within each facility so the air path is the only variable.",
